WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 4: Making Things.

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.480
In this unit you will learn the
words for shapes, colours and clothes.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.540
You will make things from paper shapes —
a paper quilt, a picture, a shape animal.

4
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.180
You will talk about what people are wearing,
and dress up in pretend party costumes.

5
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.980
You will meet the short 'e' sound in hen, pen and tent.

6
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.680
Making things takes patience, and it is fun to try, try again.

7
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.480
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:38.700
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
point to shapes (square, circle, triangle, rectangle).

9
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.420
You will also name and point to colours
(red, blue, green, yellow, silver, gold…)

10
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.760
You will also name some clothes and
costumes (hat, shirt, dress, clown, king…)

11
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.520
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:59.000
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: dog, hot, top, box, fox, log.

13
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.220
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

14
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.960
The reading sequence includes Amal
Makes a Mat and Talk about Making Things.

15
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.060
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

16
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.060
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

17
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.440
The first language focus is Name your craft materials.

18
00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.860
Name one thing from your craft box.

19
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.800
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a box, an apron.

20
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.040
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

21
00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.680
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

22
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.660
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

23
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.860
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

24
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.620
You are ready to begin.

25
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:57.400
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

26
00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.940
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
